1	# Contributing
2	
3	Contributions are welcome.
4	
5	## How to Develop
6	
7	Install and build:
8	
9	```bash
10	npm install
11	npm run build
12	```
13	
14	You can run the server directly to confirm it starts (it will wait for stdin; Ctrl+C to stop):
15	
16	```bash
17	node build/index.js
18	```
19	
20	For local development, configure Rollbar either with an environment variable or a config file. Create `.rollbar-mcp.json` in the project root (or set `ROLLBAR_CONFIG_FILE` to its path) for single- or multi-project config—see the README Configuration section.
21	
22	### Run your local installation from Claude Code
23	
24	In your Claude Code MCP config (e.g. `.mcp.json`):
25	
26	```json
27	{
28	  "mcpServers": {
29	    "rollbar": {
30	      "type": "stdio",
31	      "command": "node",
32	      "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/rollbar-mcp-server/build/index.js"],
33	      "env": {
34	        "ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<project read/write access token>"
35	      }
36	    }
37	  }
38	}
39	```
40	
41	To use a config file instead, set `"ROLLBAR_CONFIG_FILE": "/path/to/.rollbar-mcp.json"` in `env` (or omit it if `.rollbar-mcp.json` is in the project root or your home directory). Add `ROLLBAR_API_BASE` to `env` if you need a custom Rollbar API endpoint (e.g. `"ROLLBAR_API_BASE": "https://rollbar-dev.example.com/api/1"`).
42	
43	### Run your local installation from your IDE
44	
45	1. Open **Cursor Settings** (Cmd+, or File → Preferences).
46	2. Go to **Cursor Settings → Features → MCP** (or search for “MCP”).
47	3. Edit the MCP config and add a server that runs your local build:
48	
49	```json
50	{
51	  "mcpServers": {
52	    "rollbar": {
53	      "type": "stdio",
54	      "command": "node",
55	      "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/rollbar-mcp-server/build/index.js"],
56	      "env": {
57	        "ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<project read/write access token>"
58	      }
59	    }
60	  }
61	}
62	```
63	
64	Replace `/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/rollbar-mcp-server` with the real path to your clone. To use a config file instead, set `"ROLLBAR_CONFIG_FILE": "/path/to/.rollbar-mcp.json"` in `env`. Save and restart Cursor (or reload the window) so the new server is picked up. In a new Agent/Composer chat, the Rollbar tools (e.g. `list-projects`, `get-item-details`) will be available.
65	
66	### Run your local installation from VS Code
67	
68	In your `.vscode/mcp.json`:
69	
70	```json
71	{
72	  "servers": {
73	    "rollbar": {
74	      "type": "stdio",
75	      "command": "node",
76	      "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/rollbar-mcp-server/build/index.js"],
77	      "env": {
78	        "ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<project read/write access token>"
79	      }
80	    }
81	  }
82	}
83	```
84	
85	You can use `ROLLBAR_CONFIG_FILE` in `env` instead of `ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN` for config-file-based setup.
86	
87	## Testing
88	
89	Test an individual tool with the MCP inspector. List tools:
90	
91	```bash
92	npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector --cli -e ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=$TOKEN node build/index.js --method tools/list --debug
93	```
94	
95	Call a tool (e.g. `list-projects` or `get-item-details`):
96	
97	```bash
98	npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector --cli -e ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=$TOKEN node build/index.js --method tools/call --tool-name list-projects --debug
99	npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector --cli -e ROLLBAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=$TOKEN node build/index.js --method tools/call --tool-name get-item-details --tool-arg counter=2455389 --debug
100	```
101	
102	Replace `$TOKEN` with your Rollbar access token (or use a config file and set `ROLLBAR_CONFIG_FILE` in the env).
103	
104	The full e2e suite (`npm run test:e2e`) runs two scripts: the npx-install test (no token needed) and the get-item-details test. If `ROLLBAR_E2E_READ_TOKEN` is not set, the get-item-details test is skipped and the suite still passes. To run that test, set `ROLLBAR_E2E_READ_TOKEN` to a read-scope project access token for a Rollbar project that has items, including an item with counter #8.
105	

